Z||000000||NEWCOMER||12-27-2000||11:36 PM||||DOES ANYONE KNOW IF THERE ARE ANY ENGINE UPGRADES OUT THERE I AM IN THE PROCESS OF BUYING AND BUILDING A FIERO GT PLEASE HELP<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||12-27-2000||11:49 PM||||You don't have to shout (please turn caps lock off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )!<P>Yes, there are several engine upgrades available, and they have been discussed at some length here on the forum.  Some of the more popular swaps include 60-degree V6's (typically 3.1- & 3.4-liter), 90-degree V6's (such as 3800 & 3800 SC), and SBC V8's.<P>Do a search through the forum archives, and you'll find lots of reading material.<P>BTW, welcome aboard  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <P>  ||||reg||6
Z||000002||NEWCOMER||12-27-2000||11:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NEWCOMER:<BR><B>DOES ANYONE KNOW IF THERE ARE ANY ENGINE UPGRADES OUT THERE I AM IN THE PROCESS OF BUYING AND BUILDING A FIERO GT PLEASE HELP</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> I am really looking for bolt on and does anyone know of a web page I can go to and find these things<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Coconut||12-28-2000||02:16 AM||||You've FOUND the web page where you can go to and find these things...... like my bud Stugood says, do a search thru the threads, you will find a wealth of information right here! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Welcome to The Best source of info for the Fiero.<P>Cruisin, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||12
Z||000004||Predator||12-28-2000||07:37 AM||||You can also check out <A HREF="http://www.design1systems.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.design1systems.com</A>  and see their Turbo kit for the V6. It is a bolt on. I bought one and Kevin the owner is very nice and willing to work with you on any questions. He says that the StageII kit produces around 225 hp, but I cannot confirm it other than it is a lot more powerful than it was before. It is cool, because everyone thinks it is a stock Fiero, until they get a good look at the taillights that is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.usefulcomputerinfo.com/Fiero4.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000005||2M4 Dale||12-28-2000||08:39 AM||||You could start with a hypertech chip from the Fiero store or a set of headers and hi-performance exhaust.......then maybe a set of low drag pulleys. Don't forget an upgraded ignition system...ACCEL makes some goodies I think. K&N filters improve performance too.<P>The Fiero Store Link<BR> <A HREF="http://www.leaderind.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.leaderind.com/</A> <P>||||reg||14
